From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mpl: annealing stops once its best result stops improving

Every annealing run took its full 2000 steps. A run now stops when its
best result has not improved for a fifth of its budget.

Replayed from the improvement traces of every run mpl made on 25 ORFS
designs (asap7, gf180, nangate45), against the full budget:

  runs                 steps kept   cost loss: median   p95     worst
  cluster placement    59%                     0.00%    0.01%   0.19%
  macro placement      28%                     0.00%    0.00%   0.00%
  tilings              25%                     0.00%    0.00%   9.62%

A tenth of the budget cost up to 9.85% on a cluster placement. The one
tiling outlier loses the same at any patience from 300 steps up.

Not upstreamed; retires at the //:bump onto an OpenROAD that has it.

---
diff --git a/src/mpl/src/SimulatedAnnealingCore.cpp b/src/mpl/src/SimulatedAnnealingCore.cpp
index bd828582b8..bd500bdb2e 100644
--- a/src/mpl/src/SimulatedAnnealingCore.cpp
+++ b/src/mpl/src/SimulatedAnnealingCore.cpp
@@ -722,7 +722,15 @@ void SimulatedAnnealingCore<T>::fastSA()
 
   updateBestResult(cost);
 
-  while (step <= max_num_step_) {
+  // Stop once the best result has not improved for a fifth of the
+  // budget: the temperature by then is too low to leave the basin, and
+  // the remaining steps only cost time. Replayed over 25 ORFS designs'
+  // annealing traces, a fifth cost at most 0.19% of a cluster placement's
+  // cost; a tenth cost up to 9.9%.
+  const int patience = std::max(1, max_num_step_ / 5);
+  int last_best_step = 0;
+
+  while (step <= max_num_step_ && step - last_best_step <= patience) {
     for (int i = 0; i < num_perturb_per_step_; i++) {
       saveState();
       perturb();
@@ -738,6 +746,7 @@ void SimulatedAnnealingCore<T>::fastSA()
       if ((!is_best_result_valid_ || is_valid) && found_new_best_result) {
         updateBestResult(cost);
         is_best_result_valid_ = is_valid;
+        last_best_step = step;
       }
 
       const float delta_cost = cost - pre_cost;
